Credits
-------

The functional validation suite under `validation/asm/` is adapted from the
**AJIT processor project** (IIT Bombay), specifically its `ajit32`
instruction-level verification suite:

    https://github.com/adhuliya/ajit-toolchain
    https://github.com/adhuliya/ajit-toolchain/tree/master/tests/verification/ajit32

Individual test files carry their original author credit inline. Authors of
the adapted tests, in addition to Neha Karanjkar and Madhav Desai above:

- Piyush P. Soni
- Titto Thomas
- Aniket Deshmukh
- Ashfaque Ahammed

See `validation/README.md` and `compliance/README.md` for details on which
tests were adapted as-is, which were extended for this project's own
quad-precision floating-point support, and a few specific, documented
divergences from AJIT's own reference results.

`compiler/compile_c.sh` (the C-test build pipeline) follows the compile/
link/hex-dump/objdump sequence of the AJIT project's own
`tools/scripts/compileToSparc.py` and `cToSparc.py`, written by Madhav Desai
and Neha Karanjkar. The bundled `sparc-elf-gcc` cross-compiler itself
(`compiler/sparc-elf-toolchain-i386.zip`) is also from that same project's
prebuilt toolchain.
